BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 325.52 Tm (filing can zero out a site that cost more than a year to sign.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 310.30 Tm (Weather and the non-conforming rulebook combine into the second trap. Business Breakdown walks through Elena's) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 295.07 Tm (storm loss: grandfathered non-conforming signs lose their protection if reconstruction runs above roughly 50% of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 279.85 Tm (replacement value, so instead of rebuilding, the damage was repaired and every cost documented, because a fresh build) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 264.62 Tm (would have voided the protection and, as the narrator put it, "She could not replace it" [exXUEqaAB2k @ 00:11:18].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 249.40 Tm (Wind is the routine killer. A 50-foot backlit fuel-sign vinyl blew out twice, each time with a rented lift, until a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 234.17 Tm (breathable mesh replacement survived later storms [r6MxdTpj3sg @ 00:04:51]. Justin Booher reports wind frames) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 218.95 Tm (blowing out vinyl even with a self-promo underneath, which is why Booher prefers metal faces, especially on remote) Tj ET
